  "final_message": "Failed payments were never retried because `due_for_retry` filtered invoices on the status `\"opened\"`, but the billing code only ever uses `\"open\"`. The filter matched nothing, so the engine never called `collect` on a due invoice, and subscriptions stayed `past_due`.\n\n**Fix:** `billing/dunning.py`, in `due_for_retry`, changed `invoice[\"status\"] == \"opened\"` to `== \"open\"`.\n\n**Verification:** `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` passes (24 tests). The existing tests don't cover the retry path, so I didn't add a regression test or run an end-to-end decline scenario. Confirming the retry-and-escalate flow end to end would be a good next step.\n\n**Answer file:** `answer.json` in the repo root contains `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.\n\nI didn't commit anything.",
